# Project objective

Build:

- a **single Ada executable** (`eml`) that is both a **compiler** and an **interpreter**
- a **VS Code extension** for `.mxeml` / `.teml` / `.eml` (declarative editing; see `eml-vscode` rule)

The compiler reads one of four input formats (`.mxeml`, `.teml`, `.eml`, `.beml`) and emits stack EML text, binary `.beml`, JavaScript, C, native binaries (`exe`, `lib`, `dynamiclib`), or .NET sources/DLLs/exes (`csharp`, `csharplib`, `csharpdll`, `csharplibdll`, `csharpexe`, `fsharp`, `visualbasic`, `dotil`, …). The interpreter runs any of those inputs via `eml run`. CLI: `eml-cli`. CI/releases: `eml-ci`.

Do not implement code unless the user asks for that specific chunk. Keep future extensions out of the current design unless requested.

## Domain

All evaluation is in the **complex numbers** (principal branch of `ln` / `exp`, matching the EML paper).

## Naming

The paper (`docs/All elementary functions from a single operator.html`) calls the operator `eml` (Exp-Minus-Log):

`eml(x, y) = exp(x) - ln(y)`

This project names the operator and format **EML** and writes it as `eml(x, y)`, matching the paper.

The local clone folder may still be named `elm`. Do not rename that folder or anything outside this repository.

## File types

| Extension | Role |
|---|---|
| `.mxeml` | mathematical source expression (operators, functions, constants, `eml(x, y)`) |
| `.teml` | nested EML tree text (`1` and `eml(S, S)` only) |
| `.eml` | textual stack IR (`ONE` / `EML` with optional header comments) |
| `.beml` | packed-bit binary stack IR |
| `.tokens` | dump from `eml tokenize` |
| `.syntaxtree` | dump from `eml parse` (default mermaid) |

